field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.8
field_pull_wraps 80
# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-10-28 stream, 70.9 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on the build where the optical flow is
# planned by the present step run ahead (c3d3e1e). The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 329 times (278
# an hour) and stalled for 100 ms or more 71 times (60 an hour), in 119 bursts, 47 of them with a
# stall, and with no periodic stretch. The lock released 23 times, 19.5 an hour, at 1141.01,
# 1276.40, 1277.08, 1384.15, 1450.63 s, then 6 times in 7 s, 1478.26 to 1485.36 s, where the game
# hitched 14 times in 20 s with no stall, then at 1685.04, 1722.34, 1743.28, 2021.66, 2030.88,
# 2033.16, 2297.21, 2363.78, 2477.63, 2679.19, 4128.96 and 4231.16 s. The worst blend run, 42
# presents in the field, sits at 2477.5 s after two hitches of up to 41 ms. Of the 89 moves on
# the replay, 24 of them late, 26 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 47.848 s, from the 2570
# marked frames in its first 42 s, all on time within 0.37 ms of that offset (p90). The video
# runs 4338 s with no holes and opens on gameplay in a room in town (marked). Its last 80 s are
# the inventory, a book being read and the sleep wheel, then 10 s of gameplay; the cut ends where
# the inventory opens, 4305.0 s of log time (video 4257 s), and starts at the video's first
# frame, 47.8 s. Inside the cut, 27 seconds in 27 runs fall out of the 60 fps regime, each a
# single hitch second (two in one run at 4164 s).
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line reads synth 0.8% against 0.8%, worst run 39 against 42, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and
# pull wraps 77 against 80. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, blends are 2166
# against 2160, repeats 601 against 602, skips 165 against 167, pull wraps 67.7 an hour against
# 67.7 and the worst run 42 against 42. The replay makes 89 moves, 24 late, and the field's log
# has 89, 24 late, in the window; all 23 field releases match the replay's within 0.40 ms, with
# none on one side only. The planner line reads 2065 of 2066 synthesized presents planned by the
# step against 1994 by a guessed target; in the field the window's 2160 synthesized presents
# were all planned (2084 warped from a flow handed over earlier, 76 drawn as the blend because
# the flow was handed over at that present, none unplanned).
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran. The worst run's bound holds both
# arms, so it is the dejitter arm's 42 rather than the plain replay's 39.
max_worst_run 42
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.2
min_reseeds 77
max_pull_wraps 77
compositor interp
extra_lag_ms 75
